# Presale: {{product_name}}

Stamped by chief-wiggum `/apply-pattern` (`presale`, #236). This directory is an
**experiment** — an honest pre-order checkout on a product that is not built
yet. It produces the strongest evidence class a pre-build bet can have:
**strength 5 (money)** — the class the evidence-strength floor on
`bet.py transition <bet-id> building` requires.

## Binding to the validation engine (do this BEFORE launch)

1. Register the willingness-to-pay assumption and pre-register the strength-5
   card — the threshold block is hashed into the portfolio journal at creation
   (INV-PRE-001; the verdict may only be recorded against that hash):

   ```bash
   python3 scripts/assumption.py add <bet-id> \
       --statement "at least X% of <concrete population> will pre-order at ${{price_usd}}" \
       --source financial_model --element pricing
   python3 scripts/assumption.py card <bet-id> --asm ASM-NNN \
       --method presale --metric visitor_to_preorder_rate_pct \
       --comparator ">=" --value <X> --sample-min <N> \
       --cost-estimate-usd <traffic + processing budget> --evidence-strength 5
   ```

2. Wire `checkout.js`'s endpoint (`{{checkout_endpoint}}`) to a **real** payment
   provider session (INV-PRE-004: money means money — a simulated charge is
   click evidence and invalidates the strength-5 claim). Set `data-cohort` per
   launch batch.

3. Launch, then record the verdict only against the original hash:

   ```bash
   python3 scripts/assumption.py verdict <bet-id> TC-NNN \
       --result <measured rate> --sample-n <visitors> --verdict <validated|falsified>
   ```

## Honesty rules (the invariant cluster, patterns/presale/)

- Not-built-yet, the price, and the delivery window (**{{delivery_window}}**)
  stay visible ABOVE the payment step (INV-PRE-003).
- The metric is a **per-cohort conversion rate** — cumulative preorder/revenue
  totals are rejected by the vanity-metric lint (INV-PRE-002).
- **Refund-on-kill** (INV-PRE-005): if the bet is killed or pivoted before
  delivery, refund every pre-order per the stated policy ("{{refund_policy}}"),
  and count the outstanding obligation as wind-down cost in the harvest check
  (`bet.json harvest_inputs.wind_down_cost_usd`).
